KNOWLEDGE = """
SwipeX is a job-search app with three kinds of accounts: job seeker, recruiter and admin.

JOB SEEKER TABS
- Discover: swipe a job card right to save it (Liked), left to skip it. The Undo button brings the last card back. Arrow keys also work.
- Jobs: search and filter jobs. Chips: MNC, Startup, New startup, Remote, Fresher-friendly, Low competition, Last 7 days, Internships, Apprenticeships. "Verified only" is on by default and shows only jobs from verified companies. Turning it off shows everything except rejected companies, with a warning on unverified ones. The list checks for new jobs every minute and shows a banner when there are new ones.
- Companies: search any company. SwipeX shows its trust level, public facts, open jobs, recent news and an optional AI summary. The "Search the web" option finds jobs, photos, videos and news for any company name.
- Picks: Liked jobs and Skipped jobs. Skipped jobs are cleared automatically after 15 days.
- Applications: every job by status: Saved, Applied, Shortlisted, Interview, Rejected.
- Profile: headline, skills, experience, portfolio links, Resumes (up to 5 PDFs, 5 MB each, one default), and Application details (phone, links, education, work authorization, notice period, CTC in lakhs per year, default cover letter).

APPLYING
- Jobs posted on SwipeX by recruiters: open the job and choose a resume, then Apply now. The recruiter sees your profile and resume.
- Official listings come from the company's own job board (Greenhouse, Lever or Ashby). You apply on the company's site. Use "Review and autofill" to fill the form with the SwipeX Autofill Chrome extension, check every field, and press Submit yourself. Then confirm "Yes, I applied" in SwipeX.
- The extension is installed in Chrome from chrome://extensions with Developer mode on and "Load unpacked" on the extension folder. It fills name, email, phone, links, education, resume and cover letter. It never presses Submit and never answers diversity questions. AI answers for extra questions are optional and use only the question and a few non-personal facts.

SAFETY
- Each job page has a Safety check. Real employers never ask for money (registration, training or security fees), Aadhaar, PAN, bank details or OTPs. Be careful with WhatsApp-only or Telegram-only contact, personal Gmail addresses, guaranteed income, and offers without an interview.
- Check the company on its own website. Unverified companies show a warning.

RECRUITERS
- Workspace: set up the company, request verification (an admin approves), post jobs (full-time, internship, apprenticeship, part-time, contract), close or reopen jobs and review applicants (shortlist, interview, reject). Postings that ask candidates for money are blocked.

OTHER
- The sun/moon button switches light and dark themes.
- Search other portals buttons open LinkedIn, Indeed, Naukri, Internshala and Apprenticeship India searches in a new tab.
"""